Package: qdev-host
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: out-of-process PCI devices for stock QEMU (vfio-user) with Display1 export
 qdev-host runs a device model as a separate process and attaches it to an
 unmodified QEMU through vfio-user-pci. Device models are plugins; the first
 one, tb-vga, is a hot-pluggable display whose output is exported over
 QEMU's own org.qemu.Display1 D-Bus protocol (QSM Direct compatible) and can
 be scanned out on a real monitor (DRM/KMS, zero-copy). libvfio-user is
 bundled as a private library.

Package: qdev-host-pve
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, qdev-host (>= ${source:Version}), python3,
 qemu-server (>= 9), pve-manager (>= 9), pve-ui-overlays (>= 0.1.0)
Description: Proxmox VE integration for qdev-host devices
 qdevctl adds qdev-host devices to VMs on a stock Proxmox VE node: it keeps
 per-VM device definitions, installs a guest hookscript that starts the
 device processes and hot-plugs them when the VM starts, hot-adds and
 hot-removes devices on running VMs through the node's own QEMU monitor
 API, and reconnects a QSM Direct console to the device display. The VM
 Hardware panel of the web UI lists, adds and removes the devices (an overlay
 rendered by pve-ui-overlays, backed by the ticket-authorised node service
 qdev-host-api).
